-- NEWER VGM SEGA/Atlus — Section 10 part B (Jet Set Radio Future)
--
-- Source: reference/NEWER VGM Sound Sources - SEGAAtlus.csv lines 1582-1858.
-- 1 game record, ~273 usage rows. Second half of Section 10 (10a covered
-- JSR + E3 Prototype).
--
-- JSRF (Xbox, 2002) — composers per CSV: Hideki Naganuma, Richard Jacques,
-- Tomonori Sawada, B.B. Rights, Deavid Soul, The Latch Brothers. Heavy
-- cross-media sampling continues from the original JSR.
--
-- Verbatim preservations (Rule 2):
--   - "Interpolation: Prince - Housequake" (row 1) — drum pattern quote.
--   - "Live Recording: Hideki Naganuma (Vocals)" with "Guitar Interpolation
--     & ""OOWAP!""" in preset preserving the quoted vocal sample.
--   - "Live Recording: ? (Session guitarist) — Electric Bass/Guitar" —
--     identity-unknown session guitarist using em-dash to disambiguate
--     from the question-mark-in-parens uncertainty marker.
--   - Cross-media samples: The Chemical Brothers (5x), The Crystal Method,
--     Fatboy Slim, The Meters, Paula Abdul (reused from JSR), The Shirelles,
--     Stretch & Vern, plus TV/film samples (Babylon 5, Bob Dole debate,
--     Forever Knight, The X-Files "Fight For The Future").
--   - "Sample: Bob Dole - Clinton v. Dole First Presidental Debate" (T1589)
--     preserves the contributor's spelling "Presidental" verbatim.
--   - "EMU Systems" (T1699-1700) preserved distinct from existing "E-MU
--     Systems" (hyphenated) — different strings per Rule 2.
--   - "Sonic Foundry & Sounds Good" (T1752-1753) preserved distinct from
--     existing "Sonic Foundry/Sounds Good" (slash). Two further variants
--     "Sonic Foundry" (alone) and "Sonic Foundry & Hook Up" also created.
--   - "Discovery FIrm" (T1690-1691, capital I) merges via NOCASE with
--     existing "Discovery Firm" — no new manufacturer row.
--   - "Roland " (T1731, trailing space) merges via NOCASE — no duplicate.
--   - "日本語取扱説明書 CD-ROM" (T1746-1751) preserved as product name —
--     Japanese title for SF's ACID demo CD bundled with the JP localization.
--   - "Sonic Foundry & Hook Up / 日本語取扱説明書 CD-ROM" T1748's preset
--     "Riff 13 32-03\n" had an embedded CSV newline; newline dropped.
--   - "BS 2000 - The Scrappy (The Latch Brothers Remix)" (T1753) — Beastie
--     Boys side-project remixed by the in-game Latch Brothers.

